# Testing Conventions

**Trigger**: Auto-applied to test files.

## Testing Pyramid

| Layer | Tool | Targets | Speed |
|-------|------|---------|-------|
| Unit | Vitest | Utilities, validators, pure functions, types | Fast |
| Component | Vitest + Testing Library | Client Components, hooks | Fast |
| Integration | Vitest | Route Handlers, Server Actions (isolated) | Medium |
| E2E | Playwright | User flows, auth, async Server Components, production builds | Slow |

## File Naming

**Co-locate tests next to source files** with `.test.` suffix:

```
src/lib/
  auth.ts
  auth.test.ts
  utils.ts
  utils.test.ts
src/app/
  api/auth/register/
    route.ts
    route.test.ts
src/components/
  ui/button.tsx
  ui/button.test.tsx
tests/e2e/
  login.spec.ts
  onboarding.spec.ts
```

**E2E tests** go in `tests/e2e/` (not co-located) since they test across file boundaries.

## Vitest Unit Tests

**Test pure functions with input/output assertions**:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

describe('cn', () => {
  it('merges conditional classes', () => {
    expect(cn('base', true && 'active')).toBe('base active');
  });

  it('handles falsy values', () => {
    expect(cn('base', false && 'active', null, undefined)).toBe('base');
  });
});
```

**Test validators with boundary cases**:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { validateEmail } from '@/lib/validators';

describe('validateEmail', () => {
  it.each([
    ['user@example.com', true],
    ['invalid', false],
    ['', false],
  ])('%s -> %s', (email, expected) => {
    expect(validateEmail(email)).toBe(expected);
  });
});
```

## Testing Route Handlers

**Test the handler directly with real database**:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { POST } from './route';
import { prisma } from '@/lib/db';

describe('POST /api/auth/register', () => {
  it('returns 400 when email is missing', async () => {
    const req = { json: () => Promise.resolve({ password: 'test' }) } as Request;
    const res = await POST(req);
    const body = await res.json();

    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
    expect(body.error).toContain('required');
  });

  it('creates user with valid data', async () => {
    const req = { json: () => Promise.resolve({ email: 'newuser@test.com', password: 'password123' }) } as Request;
    const res = await POST(req);
    const body = await res.json();

    expect(res.status).toBe(201);
    expect(body.user.email).toBe('newuser@test.com');
    
    // Clean up test data
    await prisma.user.delete({ where: { email: 'newuser@test.com' } });
  });
});
```

## Testing Server Actions

**Test the business logic with real database**:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { createItem } from '@/app/actions/create-item';
import { prisma } from '@/lib/db';

describe('createItem', () => {
  it('creates item with valid data', async () => {
    const formData = new FormData();
    formData.append('name', 'Test Item');

    const result = await createItem(formData);
    expect(result).toEqual({ success: true });
    
    // Clean up test data
    await prisma.item.delete({ where: { name: 'Test Item' } });
  });
});
```

## Testing Client Components

**Use Testing Library for client-side interaction testing**:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';
import { LoginPage } from '@/app/(auth)/login/page';

describe('LoginPage', () => {
  it('shows error on invalid credentials', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    render(<LoginPage />);

    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Email'), 'test@example.com');
    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Password'), 'wrong');
    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /sign in/i }));

    expect(await screen.findByText(/invalid/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Async Server Components

**Do NOT unit test async Server Components with Vitest** — they require the full Next.js runtime. Test them via E2E with Playwright:

```typescript
// tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('dashboard loads user data', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: /dashboard/i })).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Mocking Strategies

**Use the local database and real credentials for testing.** Only mock external services (LLM APIs, HTTP scraping).

**Mock external services, not your own code or database**:

```typescript
// GOOD — mock LLM provider (external API)
vi.mock('@/lib/ai/provider', () => ({
  getProvider: () => ({
    completeStructured: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ /* mock response */ }),
  }),
}));

// GOOD — mock HTTP requests for scraping (external service)
vi.mock('node-fetch', () => ({
  default: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ /* mock response */ }),
}));

// BAD — do NOT mock the database
// vi.mock('@/lib/db', () => ({ prisma: { /* ... */ } }));

// BAD — do NOT mock authentication with fake users
// vi.mock('next-auth', () => ({
//   auth: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ user: { email: 'test@example.com' } }),
// }));
```

**Use real test credentials from seeded database:**

```typescript
// GOOD - use real admin credentials for testing
const adminCredentials = {
  email: 'admin@thetell.com',
  password: 'password123',
};

// GOOD - use real analyst credentials for testing
const analystCredentials = {
  email: 'analyst@thetell.com',
  password: 'password123',
};
```

**Reset mocks between tests**:

```typescript
import { beforeEach, vi } from 'vitest';

beforeEach(() => {
  vi.clearAllMocks();
});
```

## Coverage Expectations

| Category | Target | Rationale |
|----------|--------|-----------|
| Utilities / validators | 100% | Pure functions, easy to cover fully |
| Route Handlers | 80%+ | Cover success, validation errors, and error paths |
| Client Components | 80%+ | Cover render and key interactions |
| Server Actions | 70%+ | Test logic; leave integration to E2E |
| Server Components | E2E only | Require full runtime |
| E2E critical paths | All happy paths + 1 error path each | Login, onboarding, key user flows |

## Running Tests

```powershell
# Unit + component tests
pnpm exec vitest run

# Watch mode
pnpm exec vitest

# Single test file
pnpm exec vitest run src/lib/utils.test.ts

# E2E tests
pnpm exec playwright test

# Specific E2E test
pnpm exec playwright test login
```
